111
00:07:45,285 --> 00:07:48,020
So what is a composite profile?

112
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:51,980
A traditional profile is made up of one day of data.

113
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:58,920
However, sometimes we wish to have a flexible profile that can illustrate an auction that

114
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:03,860
includes multiple profiles or even a time slice within a day.

115
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:11,590
Any profile that is made up of several parts or multiple profiles can be deemed a composite profile.

116
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:16,620
What is important is not the definition, but rather the implications.

117
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:21,575
So very simply, traditionally, a volume profile is one day.

118
00:08:21,575 --> 00:08:25,465
It includes all the data and all the prices traded over one day.

119
00:08:25,465 --> 00:08:29,390
But you can take any, say, half an hour section of the day.

120
00:08:29,390 --> 00:08:34,515
You can take a couple of days. You can take a couple of months and create a volume profiling.

121
00:08:34,515 --> 00:08:42,860
The principle of volume profiling is to try and illustrate where trade has been facilitated over a given period.

122
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:46,985
So any period that isn't a day is a composite profile.

123
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:49,485
So why do we use these composite profiles?

124
00:08:49,485 --> 00:08:54,375
Well, very simply, firstly, it ensures we constantly understand the bigger picture.

125
00:08:54,375 --> 00:08:56,140
So it gives us a top-down approach.

126
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,515
What do we mean by that?

127
00:08:57,515 --> 00:09:00,820
Well, if we look at, say, a monthly volume profile,

128
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:07,390
we will see effectively how volume has been distributed over price and time over an entire month.

129
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:13,940
So it gives us a good, bigger-term perspective of what has actually gone on over the period of a month.

130
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:16,970
Then, markets have long-term memory.

131
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:24,325
So, again, sometimes we use these composite profiles to develop very unique strategies based on weekly and monthly charts.

132
00:09:24,325 --> 00:09:24,795
Why?

133
00:09:24,795 --> 00:09:25,662
Because, well, you

134
00:09:25,662 --> 00:09:27,687
might, as a day trader, you might

135
